(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF REGULATION, CENTRAL OFFICE, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/118 DOR.AML.REC.42/14.01.001/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 10, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Direction - Know Your Customer \(KYC\) Direction - Periodic Updation and V-CIP) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Periodic KYC Updation Timelines: Regulated Entities shall carry out periodic KYC updation based on customer risk categorization.) Tj
T*
(Periodic updation of Customer Due Diligence \(CDD\) shall be conducted at least once every two years for high-risk customers,) Tj
T*
(at least once every eight years for medium-risk customers, and at least once every ten years for low-risk customers.) Tj
T*
(2. Re-KYC for Non-Risk Customers: Where there is no change in KYC information, a self-declaration from the customer submitted) Tj
T*
(through internet banking, mobile app, ATM, or email shall suffice for periodic updation.) Tj
T*
(3. Video-based Customer Identification Process \(V-CIP\): V-CIP is an alternate method of digital customer verification.) Tj
T*
(The V-CIP infrastructure must ensure live, real-time audio-visual interaction conducted by an authorized official of the RE.) Tj
T*
(The official must verify the live photograph against the Aadhaar or OVD photograph using facial recognition algorithms with) Tj
T*
(a match confidence score exceeding 90 percent.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 1136 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
